      "text": "It blasts fireballs of over 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit out of its arms. Its breath also sears and sizzles.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "They dwell in volcanic craters. According to what is known, a single pair of male and female Magmortar lives in one volcano.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "From its arm, it launches fireballs hotter than 3,500 degrees Fahrenheit. Its arm starts to melt when it fires a whole barrage.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "There are still quite a few factories that rely on the flames provided by Magmortar to process metals.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Magmortar takes down its enemies by shooting fireballs, which burn them to a blackened crisp. It avoids this method when hunting prey.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Magmortar inhales deeply, the fire burning in its belly intensifies, rising in temperature to over 3,600 degrees Fahrenheit.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Living in the crater of a volcano has caused this Pokémon’s body to resemble its environment— it has an organ similar to a magma chamber.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use of a strange item caused this Pokémon to evolve. Fireballs launched from the ends of its tubelike arms are hot enough to melt an iron pot in an instant.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
